SCOPE -- WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES NOT COVER
-----------------------------------------

CC BY 4.0 applies to the documentation content. Three categories are excluded:

1.  The FracSTAT software itself. The desktop application's source code lives
    in a separate repository and is distributed under the MIT License:

        https://github.com/sachi5908/FracSTAT

    Reuse of code follows the MIT terms there, not CC BY 4.0. The small amount
    of site machinery in this repository (script.js, style.css, admin.html) is
    likewise offered under the MIT License so it can be reused without the
    attribution requirement that applies to the prose.

2.  Trademarks and logos. The FracSTAT name and logo are not licensed under
    CC BY 4.0. You may use them to refer to the project, but not in a way that
    suggests endorsement of a derivative work.

3.  Third-party material. Where this documentation reproduces figures,
    equations, or excerpts attributed to published sources -- for example the
    Mauldon et al. (2001) circular-scanline method -- those items remain under
    their original terms. Cite the original publication rather than relying on
    this license.


